# …except the two tiny documents SafeDocumentTextExtractor needs. The rest of
# test-fixtures/ is a 46MB corpus regenerated with live MiniMax calls, which no
# CI run can reproduce — so those two suites failed on every run for want of a
# 3.7KB PDF and a 2.2KB DOCX. These are generated deterministically by
# scripts/e2e/lib/docwriters.mjs (jsPDF + JSZip, no network, no model) and carry
# only the marker names the tests assert on.
!test-fixtures/profiles/p01/resume.pdf
!test-fixtures/profiles/p03/resume.docx

traces/
traces2/
traces3/
--help/
.remember/
fixtures/
# ...but NOT test fixtures that suites import. The blanket `fixtures/` above swept up
# electron/**/__tests__/fixtures/*, which the "remove tracked files per updated
# .gitignore" cleanup then deleted — leaving 4 test files importing modules that no
# longer existed. Both lines are required and must stay in this order: git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so the directory itself has to be re-included
# before its contents can be.
!electron/**/__tests__/fixtures/
!electron/**/__tests__/fixtures/**
# Same sweep deleted tests/fixtures/modes/* (73 files) in 6f8e3329 — the mode
# reference-file corpus that CustomModes / ModePersonaScenarios / Seminar /
# ModeFixtureIntegrity / ModeBleedingMatrix import. That turned ~120 suite
# cases into unconditional ENOENT failures on every fresh checkout. Restored
# from 6f8e3329~1 (2026-08-11) and re-included here so the cleanup cannot
# recur. Same two-line pattern as above: re-include the directory first, then
# its contents.
!tests/fixtures/
!tests/fixtures/**
tools/

